Hi Jeff:

	I may have missed earlier messages in this thread. Is your problem
specifically
with Gentoo? I have no experience with that particular flavour. As to
logging, if you set
your log level to info, the log messages will appear in /var/log/messages
with most distributions.
Put a rule at the end of each chain (i.e. FORWARD, INPUT, USER) to see what
is dropping
through your rules. Something like:

$IPTABLES -A FORWARD -j LOG --log-level info  --log-prefix "FW INPUT  "
$IPTABLES -A FORWARD -j DROP

	You don't show any rules for forwarding. Every DNAT Rule needs a forward
rule to
go with it unless the default policy is accept (Not Recommended!). Have you
tried setting
up tcpdump or ethereal to watch the external and internal side to see what
traffic is going
through?

Stu.........


