I am at the end of my rope, I have been able to forward pcanywhere ports to
a local machine with mandrake linux 8.1 using iptables version 1.2.2 with
the following rules:

echo 1 > /proc/sys/net/ipv4/ip_forward
iptables -t nat -A PREROUTING -p tcp --dport 5631 -i eth0 -j DNAT --to
192.168.10.247:5631
iptables -t nat -A PREROUTING -p tcp --dport 5632 -i eth0 -j DNAT --to
192.168.10.247:5632
iptables -t nat -A PREROUTING -p udp --dport 5631 -i eth0 -j DNAT --to
192.168.10.247:5631
iptables -t nat -A PREROUTING -p udp --dport 5632 -i eth0 -j DNAT --to
192.168.10.247:5632

this gives me the following table when I type iptables -t nat -L:

Chain PREROUTING (policy ACCEPT)
target     prot opt source               destination
DNAT       tcp  --  anywhere             anywhere           tcp dpt:5631
to:192.168.10.247:5631
DNAT       tcp  --  anywhere             anywhere           tcp dpt:5632
to:192.168.10.247:5632
DNAT       udp  --  anywhere             anywhere           udp dpt:5631
to:192.168.10.247:5631
DNAT       udp  --  anywhere             anywhere           udp dpt:5632
to:192.168.10.247:5632

Chain POSTROUTING (policy ACCEPT)
target     prot opt source               destination

Chain OUTPUT (policy ACCEPT)
target     prot opt source               destination


Further, I have enabled every possible option in the kernel for nat and
every possible tcp/ip option in the kernel and built it as a monolithic
kernel.  Just to be thorough I will include my .config file below for the
kernel. (I did this to be thorough, I just want to make it clear that I have
all the necessary options enabled in my kernel...if not however I would love
to be told that I am wrong :)  I also have to stress it has nothing to do
with my iptable conditions as listed earlier, as it has worked for me and
continues to work for me on other machines, and the only way it wouldnt
continue to work is if the iptables syntax or something similar changed
between iptables 1.2.2 and 1.2.6a.  Is there any info I left out?  Is there
anything else I need to install?  I would give log files also, but I am
unsure how iptables logging works...if someone can help me with that too I
would appreciate it.  I have found the documentation pretty poor when it
comes to explaining logging features as there only seems to be a FAQ and
howtos.  (The howtos and faq have been helpful to me with past issues
however...no flame intended)

Jeff

